# Documentation and agent guidance

- Write for teams adopting this repo as a starter, not just for the current project.
- Keep docs concise, practical, and aligned with the real workspace layout and commands.
- Root docs should describe repo-wide behavior; app docs should add only app-specific guidance.
- If app purpose, commands, or starter workflow changes, update the matching README and guidance files in the same change.
- Avoid stale template language from framework generators once the starter has an opinionated baseline of its own.
